      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-146295",
      ":question/problem": "Suppose that $45%$ of the voting population plans to vote for candidate $A$ in the upcoming mayoral election. A random sample of size $n = 20$ is taken from the population and asked about their voting preference.\n\nWhat is the mean and variance of $p^(^)$, the proportion of voters in the sample that plan to vote for candidate $A$? Round your answers to $4$ decimal places where appropriate.\n\n*Hint: You may assume that the population size is significantly larger than the sample size.*\n\n> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question."
    },
